cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, please cite it as below, naming the release version you used."
type: dataset
title: "DGX Spark benchmarks: open-weight models as autonomous coding agents on 128 GB unified memory"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
authors:
  - family-names: Rajendran
    given-names: Adithya
    website: "https://adithya-rajendran.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Adithya-Rajendran/dgx-spark-benchmarks"
url: "https://github.com/Adithya-Rajendran/dgx-spark-benchmarks"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Measured results for open-weight language models running as autonomous coding agents (Claude Code, headless,
  in network-isolated microVMs) on an NVIDIA GB10 machine with 128 GB unified memory (DGX Spark class).
  Includes per-attempt outcomes on 18 post-training-cutoff Python bug fixes graded with hidden tests and an
  11-task SWE-bench Pro subset, plus token, tool-call, time, GPU energy and memory measurements, 1 Hz
  telemetry, serving-speed and engine-tuning results, and the exact server configurations.
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - LLM evaluation
  - open-weight models
  - local inference
  - DGX Spark
  - NVIDIA GB10
  - SWE-bench
  - energy
